# scripts/leak-check.allowed-addresses
#
# Well-known public address constants that the leak check lets stay in the
# tree because the code, its tests and its documentation must name them:
# the cloud metadata endpoints that the SSRF guards always refuse. They
# identify no machine of the operator. One literal address per line; a line
# of a file passes when removing these literals leaves no address match.
# This file itself is excluded from the scan (see scripts/leak-check.exclude).
#
# Keep this list to public constants. Never add a private, tailnet or
# internal address of any machine.
169.254.169.254
fd00:ec2::254
